    37	   median exposures-per-night quantiles (10/50/90) = (1.0, 1.0, 2.0); K=0 and
    38	   K=1 windows have identical exposures-per-night for 103/103 targets; K=2 is
    39	   1–2. The three windows are valid magnitude-matched replicates, but the
    40	   plan's "10/50/90th percentile of exposures-per-night" stratification does
    41	   not stratify; the completeness surface's exposure axis (bins 1/1.5/2/3/5)
    42	   is populated almost entirely at 1–2.
    43	2. **Native variability dominates detection-only P4.** 342/928 pool windows
    44	   are published `confirmed` (+76 candidate); 53/119 gen1 nominal-B windows
    45	   are confirmed. In the pilot, on confirmed windows nominal B is "confirmed"
    46	   11/13 times but recovers the injected dominant mode 2/13; on not_detected
    47	   windows 4/15 confirmed, all 4 direct recoveries. The uninjected controls
    48	   reproduce the published status 10/10. Detection-only P4 therefore mostly
    49	   measures the pool's native variability at these magnitudes; the
    50	   frequency-recovery endpoint behaves as designed.
    51	3. Arm-A confirmations that are not the dominant mode (5/15): one is another
    52	   injected mode (`best_candidate_matches_any_mode = direct`), one sits
    53	   ~1.6× the match tolerance from the sidereal alias of the dominant mode,
    54	   three are unmatched peaks with the injected frequency present in the top-15
    55	   (`any_top_peak_matches_any_mode = true`).
