   151	## D2 — TESS-truth transplant (DAV signals in real ZTF windows)
   152	
   153	- Truth: Romero+2022 (MNRAS 511, 1574; arXiv:2201.04158; 74 new DAVs,
   154	  TESS Cy1–3) + Romero+2025 (ApJ 984, 112; arXiv:2407.07260; 32 new DAVs,
   155	  Cy4–5). Published per-mode tables: period [s] + amplitude [ppt] + per-star
   156	  FAP(1/1000) limit + 20-s-cadence flags. 2025 revisions apply: NOV
   157	  retractions (TIC 261400271, 804835539, 317620456) and updated mode lists
   158	  for re-observed 2022 objects — latest published solution wins.
   159	- Truth model, not interpolation (`d2_truth_model.py`): for 120-s sampling,
   160	  DAV P < 240 s is super-Nyquist (Nyquist period 240 s) and the boxcar
   161	  integration response has its first null at P = 120 s — two distinct
   162	  boundaries, both making interpolated TESS photometry undefined in the DAV
   163	  range; the mode table is evaluated analytically at the template's real
   164	  `bjd_tdb`. Chain: ppt → mag (×1.0857e-3) → crowding: the published
   165	  amplitudes are PDCSAP, already dilution-corrected (Romero+2022 §2,
   166	  Romero+2025 §2), so no de-dilution is applied; the prespecified crowding
   167	  SENSITIVITY is the SAP-equivalent RE-dilution A × CROWDSAP (multiplication;
   168	  Amendment 2 — the pre-G3 text's "divide by CROWDSAP" would have inflated
   169	  amplitudes ~5× at the median CROWDSAP 0.19), scheduled only for
   170	  SPOC-verified targets whose CROWDSAP is on file →
   171	  de-integrate the TESS boxcar (signed sinc; REJECT modes with
   172	  |sinc| < 0.3, i.e. P < ~160 s at 120-s cadence, P < ~27 s at 20-s);
   173	  cadence precedence is algorithmic: cadence_s (an EFFECTIVE integration
   174	  time; TESS timestamps are exposure midpoints, as the signed-sinc algebra
   175	  assumes) = 20 iff the star's chosen published solution includes any "f"
   176	  (20-s) sector, else 120 →
   177	  bandpass ladder A_g/A_TESS ∈ {1.4, 1.7, 2.1} × A_r/A_g ∈
   178	  {0.70, 0.80, 0.90} — a PHENOMENOLOGICAL SENSITIVITY GRID, not a derived
   179	  physical range: the blackbody T-derivative at 11,500 K gives (1.43, 0.80)
   180	  ≈ the low rung (not band-integrated, no limb darkening, l-independent);
   181	  the ADOPTED nominal (1.7, 0.80) is the grid midpoint; DA-atmosphere
   182	  band-integrated validation of the endpoints is a stated limitation (the
   183	  ladder is non-optional — zr carries most published confirmations) →
   184	  re-integrate the ZTF 30-s boxcar analytically → compose with the FROZEN
   185	  phase protocol: one independent phase per mode; base assignment
   186	  (phase_draw = 0) seeds PCG64(TIC) and is shared across bands and across
   187	  every bandpass/de-dilution/amplitude-scale variant; the two phase-draw
   188	  sensitivity variants d ∈ {1, 2} seed PCG64(TIC·10 + d) and change ONLY
   189	  the phase vector; shared t_ref keeps the frozen two-band rule meaningful.
   190	- Windows: templates from ALL 928 stars of the published catalog (G1 fix —
   191	  the earlier 510-not-detected pool conditioned on the pipeline's own
   192	  outcome), matched by median zg mag (|Δg| ≤ 0.25, widened when thin;
   193	  flagged), K=3 per target at 10/50/90th percentile of exposures-per-night
   194	  (75% of zg nights are single-exposure; per-night median subtraction
   195	  annihilates 53% of zg data — pre-registered, stratified: risk 3).
   196	  Template matching is a TOTAL deterministic algorithm (zero analyst
   197	  discretion): candidate pool = stars with |median_zg − target_G| ≤ 0.25;
   198	  if fewer than 3, the pool widens once to ≤ 0.5; if still fewer than 3,
   199	  the pool is the 9 smallest |Δmag| stars, magnitude ties broken by
   200	  ascending source_id (pandas argsort is stable over the source_id-sorted
   201	  stats table); the pool is then sorted lexicographically by
   202	  (median exposures-per-night, source_id) — a total order, so no residual
   203	  ties — and picks are indices round-half-even(q·(n−1)) for
   204	  q ∈ {0.10, 0.50, 0.90} (numpy round). Match label recorded per target.
   205	  D2 primary detection is post-injection rule firing (detection-only);
   206	  strict frequency matching is the separate frequency-recovery estimand;
   207	  native variability in the pool is contextualized by PAIRED UNINJECTED
   208	  CONTROLS (95-prefix; stable ids indexed over the sorted 928 pool): one
   209	  control shard per unique arm-B template window. W2 stretch: fetch real
   210	  ZTF light curves at the 103 Romero positions; usable self-windows form a
   211	  SEPARATE DIAGNOSTIC arm — they do not replace or enter the nominal K=3
   212	  aggregate.
   213	- Arms: B primary (signal + real ZTF mags, real magerr), A diagnostic for
   214	  positive injections; arm-A ZERO-AMPLITUDE NULLS are the campaign's sole
   215	  confirmatory endpoint (P5, METRICS_SPEC). Gaussian-null false-alarm rate
   216	  (`FPR_Gaussian`): 1,000 arm-A zero-amplitude simulations scheduled over
   217	  the 928-window frame by deterministic cycling (serial i → sorted-pool
   218	  window i mod 928, noise seed = serial); windows repeat, seeds do not.
   219	  Verification arm: ~20 SPOC light curves prewhitened to confirm published
   220	  solutions; everything else needs metadata only.
   221	- Run matrix (22 workers ≈ 84 runs/h). CORE scheduled total ≤ 3,299 ≈
   222	  1.6 d (3,266 + the 33 Amendment-3 `cadence_alt` shards), all binding: arm B nominal (1.7/0.80) 103×3 = 309; arm A nominal
   223	  309; Gaussian nulls 1,000; paired controls ≤ 309 (unique arm-B windows);
   224	  ladder sensitivity MEDIAN-WINDOW-CONDITIONED: 8 non-nominal (R_g, R_rg)
   225	  points × 103 × 1 = 824; phase-draw sensitivity 2 × 103 = 206;
   226	  amplitude-stationarity axis (scale × {0.7, 1.3}) 2 × 103 = 206;
   227	  dominant-mode-dropout variant ≤ 103 (targets with ≥ 2 RETAINED modes;
   228	  the dropped mode is the largest-amplitude retained mode; every survivor
   229	  keeps its nominal phase — Amendment 2) — the ±30% multiplier is a LOCAL
   230	  sensitivity, not an astrophysical envelope; DAV modes can vanish outright
   231	  between epochs, which dropout probes (all sensitivity axes: median window,
   232	  arm B nominal ratios). Targets with ZERO retained modes at their cadence
   233	  cannot be positives and are excluded from the matrix (recorded in
   234	  excluded_targets.csv; the scheduled-target list is frozen in the
   235	  generation manifest and is the P4 denominator).
   236	  Stretch additions listed separately: Romero self-window diagnostic
   237	  (count set by crossmatch yield); SAP-equivalent re-dilution variant only
   238	  for the SPOC verification-arm stars (CROWDSAP comes with the downloads).
   239	  Every sensitivity contrast uses the common-subset rule (METRICS_SPEC).
   240	- Amendment 3 (mixed-cadence endpoint sensitivity, G3 round-3 ADOPT-A): the
   241	  frozen nominal cadence precedence remains `cadence_s = 20` whenever the
   242	  chosen published solution contains any `f` sector; because the completed
   243	  SPOC v3 verification identifies 33 such mixed 20-s/120-s targets, schedule
   244	  for each exactly one additional arm-B, median-window (K=1) `cadence_alt`
   245	  sensitivity shard at the nominal bandpass ratios (1.7/0.80), base phase
   246	  draw, amplitude scale 1.0, PDCSAP crowding, and no dominant-mode dropout,
   247	  evaluating the complete truth model with `cadence_s = 120` and reapplying
   248	  the signed-sinc |sinc| ≥ 0.3 rule (three modes on TIC 55650407 are thereby
   249	  rejected); `cadence_alt` is a conservative pure-120-s endpoint, not an
   250	  estimate of the stitched solution's effective cadence (the stitched bias is
   251	  S_20/S_mix, ~1.1–1.4 under plausible fit weightings, not the ~1.9 endpoint
   252	  contrast at 200 s), is compared with nominal on the same 33-target K=1
   253	  subset using common bootstrap draws, never enters nominal P4 or is pooled
   254	  with nominal surfaces, retains the scenario-invariant published-amplitude
   255	  coordinate, has its own immutable scenario code and final campaign-id
   256	  digit, and adds exactly 33 shards. Dominance is scenario-local; dropout
   257	  stays a nominal-cadence scenario (no dropout × cadence_alt crossing).
   258	- Generation discipline (Amendment 2, G3 methods findings 1–8): every
   259	  manifest row of every arm carries the fixed typed schema
   260	  (d2_truth_model.MANIFEST_COLUMNS) including an explicit immutable
   261	  `scenario` code and `n_strata_scheduled` (3 nominal, 1 single-window
   262	  sensitivity); shards are built into a staging directory under an
   263	  IN_PROGRESS sentinel from the ATTESTED per-star exposure shards (original
   264	  text tokens preserved; model evaluated on the frozen loader's parse; each
   265	  written shard re-loaded through the frozen loader and checked bitwise on
   266	  epochs), validated (index == manifest == disk, SHA identity, A/B ↔
   267	  injected-mode bijection, exactly K = {0,1,2} nominal-B replicates per
   268	  scheduled target, exact null serials), described by a generation manifest
   269	  (generation id over every input SHA + code SHAs + arguments; per-shard
   270	  SHAs; roster-report and SPOC-report SHAs) and published atomically —
   271	  there is no resume. The runner refuses unpublished generations, binds
   272	  each result's sidecar to shard SHA, result SHA, pass set, env, frozen and
   273	  campaign digests, attestation SHA and generation id, and writes a per-id
   274	  completion table; metrics verify all of it before counting a result.
   275	  Timing pilot = the builder's stratified `pilot_shard_index.txt` (~150
   276	  shards spanning every arm/scenario, window strata and amplitudes) run via
   277	  `--stars-file`; pilot outputs are never confirmatory for P4/P5.
   278	- Truth-model corrections found at implementation (2026-08-28): |sinc| ≥ 0.3
   279	  rejection corresponds to P < ~160 s at 120-s cadence (the earlier "197 s"
   280	  was the |sinc| = 0.5 point); D2 min published period is 115.9 s and 49/103
   281	  stars carry 20-s solutions, so few modes are affected. Phase protocol is
   282	  frozen above (per-mode independent; PCG64(TIC) base; PCG64(TIC·10+d)
   283	  for the two phase-draw variants). Blackbody derivative at 11,500 K gives
   284	  (1.43, 0.80) ≈ the 1.4/0.80 low rung; upper rungs cover
   285	  atmosphere-model/limb-darkening uncertainty; 1.7 is the adopted midpoint.
   286	
   287	## Metrics — see METRICS_SPEC.md (frozen before any campaign L-S run)
   288	
   289	## Execution topology
   290	
     1	# METRICS_SPEC — to be frozen at G2 (freeze = git blob SHA recorded in
     2	# GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md when the G2 panel reaches no-blocker verdicts)
     3	
     4	Implemented by `scripts/generalization/metrics_generalization.py`. Any change
     5	after the first campaign L-S run voids the prespecification and must be
     6	reported as such. v3, 2026-08-28: absorbs G2 round-2 findings (referee2,
     7	stats2, methods2, abstract lenses).
     8	
     9	## Estimand vocabulary (names are binding)
    10	
    11	Three separate response assessments; never pooled.
    12	
    13	- **detection completeness** — P(rule fires | labeled positive), reported for
    14	  BOTH denominators: `eligible_roster` (missing/unusable light curves count
    15	  as non-detections) and `usable_lightcurve` (frozen QC passed, both passes
    16	  complete). D1 denominators: the 13 paper-variable stars of the published
    17	  19-star master table (the 928-star catalog is NOT a labeled-positive
    18	  completeness denominator). D3: the 610 dSct=1 survivors. D2: injection
    19	  targets — always labeled *conditional injection-recovery efficiency of the
    20	  search stage*; D2 primary detection = post-injection rule firing
    21	  (detection-only); strict frequency matching is the separate
    22	  frequency-recovery estimand; paired controls contextualize native triggers.
    23	- **frequency-recovery completeness** — P(rule fires AND
    24	  best_candidate_matches_dominant | labeled positive AND freq-scorable AND
    25	  S_p = 1). Freq-scorable: D3 = Mo-joined with >=1 frequency and a defined
    26	  dominant amplitude (assert count == 456; "Mo-join-conditioned" label
    27	  mandatory; joined-vs-unjoined covariate table mandatory); D2 = >=1
    28	  RETAINED injected mode (from injected_modes.csv, post |sinc|>=0.3
    29	  rejection — never the original mode table); D1 = diagnostic only
    30	  (non-contemporaneous literature frequencies; see below).
    31	  S_p (per pass p): >=1 truth frequency inside pass p's search bounds
    32	  (low: [2/baseline, 48] / d; high: [24, 1440] / d); S_best = S_low OR
    33	  S_high. Known consequence stated up front: only ~10/456 D3 dominant
    34	  frequencies lie >= 24 / d, so D3 high-pass frequency recovery is a
    35	  near-empty cell and is reported as counts.
    36	  Mo-join MNAR limitation (binding statement): Mo inclusion required
    37	  SNR > 8 in Kepler photometry and is plausibly related to amplitude,
    38	  magnitude, and mode complexity; missingness for the 154 unjoined
    39	  positives is treated as informative — the frequency-recovery curve is
    40	  therefore a Mo-join-conditioned estimand, the joined-vs-unjoined
    41	  covariate table is mandatory, and DETECTION surfaces retain all 610
    42	  positives with the unjoined stars in an explicit `amp_unknown` bin so
    43	  their detection behavior is visible beside the joined sample.
    44	  The missed-vs-wrong-frequency decomposition uses matching denominators
    45	  only: P(D AND M | Y=1, F=1, S_p=1) vs P(D | Y=1, F=1, S_p=1).
    46	- **correct-frequency fraction among detected positives** —
    47	  P(best_candidate_matches_dominant | rule-1 fired, Y=1, F=1, S_p=1).
    48	  Never called purity.
    49	- **frame-specific label PPV (D3 only)** — among triggered roster members of
    50	  the weighted frame {dSct=1 census positives, dSct=0 SRS negatives; dSct=2
    51	  EXCLUDED, reported separately}: weighted fraction labeled dSct=1.
    52	  Interval: FPC-rescaled survey bootstrap (B=2000, frozen seed): the 2,314
    53	  negatives are resampled with replacement, positives held fixed (census),
    54	  and bootstrap deviations are rescaled by sqrt(1 − f) with sampling
    55	  fraction f = 2314/7292 (SRSWOR finite-population correction).
    56	  No transfer to other prevalences. Output: ppv.csv.
    57	- **negative-class trigger rate (D3)** — P(rule fires | dSct=0, the
    58	  NON-dSct COMPARISON CLASS — it contains genuine gamma Dor, rotational,
    59	  binary and other variables, which is why this is a trigger rate). Weights are
    60	  constant within the class and cancel: plain Wilson on the 2,314 sampled
    61	  negatives (no FPC — conservative). Triggered negatives adjudicated in W4
    62	  (plausible real variable vs unexplained), reported descriptively.
    63	- **Gaussian-null false-alarm rate (FPR_Gaussian, D2)** — P(confirmed |
    64	  arm-A zero-amplitude null), n = 1000; window allocation frozen as
    65	  deterministic cycling of the sorted 928-window pool (serial i -> window
    66	  i mod 928), noise seed = serial. Interval: EXACT one-sided
    67	  Clopper-Pearson upper bound at the OBSERVED event count x
    68	  (U = Beta_{0.95}(x+1, n-x)); acceptance criterion (confirmatory):
    69	  U_95(x, 1000) <= 0.005. Windows repeat; inference is conditional on the
    70	  frozen window set. FP frequency-distribution/alias audit descriptive only
    71	  below 10 events.
    72	- **native trigger rate of the template pool (D2)** — P(confirmed | paired
    73	  uninjected control window, 95-prefix). Context, not an FPR.
    74	
    75	Exact D3 sampling constants (binding): negatives inclusion probability
    76	2314/7292 (= 0.31733406...), sampling weight 7292/2314 (= 3.15125324...);
    77	never derived from rounded values.
    78	
    79	## D1 specifics
    80	
    81	Labels from the published master table (19 usable stars: 13 paper-variable,
    82	5 paper-constant, 1 transit control excluded from both classes — it is the
    83	frozen pipeline's eclipsing sanity object). D1 truth frequencies are
    84	non-contemporaneous single-epoch literature tabulations of multi-mode
    85	pulsators (observed lit-vs-ZTF offsets reach 0.6%): frequency-recovery for
    86	D1 is DIAGNOSTIC only; the D1 estimand is detection completeness.
    87	Match tolerance adds a truth-quantum term: D1 +0.0025 / d (2-decimal
    88	tables); D2/D3 +0. Validation on record (2026-08-28): the engine reproduces
    89	all five published D1 numbers (11/13 L-S, 9/13 census, 13/13 union,
    90	0 confirmed + 1 candidate among the 5 constants).
    91	
    92	## Frequency-match taxonomy (evaluate everything, then classify)
    93	
    94	Tolerance: 1.5 / baseline_days + truth-quantum. f_sid = 1.00273790935 / d
    95	(frozen, the pipeline's constant). For each detected candidate, evaluate ALL
    96	(truth mode, relation) hits across the star's full truth list:
    97	  direct       |f_cand - f_t| <= tol
    98	  harmonic     |f_cand - 2 f_t| <= tol or |f_cand - f_t/2| <= tol
    99	  window_alias |f_cand - |f_t +/- k f_sid|| <= tol, k = 1, 2
   100	Classification: no hits -> `unmatched`; hits in exactly one relation class ->
   101	that class (several DIRECT hits on different modes remain `direct`); hits in
   102	more than one relation class -> `ambiguous` (excluded from strict recovery).
   103	Named estimator columns encode both axes:
   104	`best_candidate_matches_dominant` (headline; D3 dominant Mo mode / D2
   105	largest-amplitude retained injected mode; D1 diagnostic) and
   106	`best_candidate_matches_any_mode` (secondary), plus
   107	`any_top_peak_matches_any_mode` (diagnostic over the 15 stored peaks).
   108	Chance-match calibration: truth lists permuted across stars (frozen seed
   109	20260829, 100 permutations) -> accidental direct-match rate beside every
   110	frequency-recovery table.
   111	
   112	## Detection rules and the preregistered primary family
   113	
   114	Rules (all four always reported): 1 `confirmed`, 2 `confirmed|candidate`,
   115	3 `census` (any of six frozen ratios >= 2.5), 4 `either` (1 OR 3).
   116	PRIMARY endpoints — complete tuples; everything else is pointwise
   117	descriptive sensitivity:
   118	  P1 D3 detection completeness: {D3, dSct=1 (610), eligible_roster, rule 1,
   119	     best pass, unweighted, Wilson 95%}.
   120	  P2 D3 frequency recovery: {D3, Mo-joined S_best=1 subset, usable, rule 1 +
   121	     best_candidate_matches_dominant, Wilson 95%, beside chance-match rate}.
   122	  P3 D3 negative-class trigger rate: {D3, dSct=0 (2314), rule 1, best pass,
   123	     plain Wilson}.
   124	  P4 D2 conditional injection-recovery, algebraically:
   125	     p-hat = (1/103) Σ_t (1/|K_t|) Σ_{k in K_t} y_{t,k}, where y_{t,k} = 1
   126	     iff rule 1 fires (detection-only) on target t's stratum-k nominal
   127	     (1.7/0.80, de-dilution off, phase_draw 0) arm-B shard, and K_t ⊆
   128	     {0, 1, 2} is the set of strata with a usable result. ELIGIBLE variant:
   129	     denominator all 103 targets; missing stratum counts y = 0 with
   130	     |K_t| = n_strata_scheduled (3 for the nominal scenario; 1 for the
   131	     single-window sensitivity scenarios — Amendment 2); a K_t = ∅ target
   132	     contributes 0. USABLE variant:
   133	     p-hat_u = (1/(103 − n_∅)) Σ_{t: K_t ≠ ∅} (1/|K_t|) Σ_k y_{t,k} —
   134	     K_t = ∅ targets are excluded from numerator AND denominator, with
   135	     n_∅ reported as n_targets_zero_usable_strata. The bootstrap resamples
   136	     all 103 target labels with the common draw matrix for both variants;
   137	     a resampled-in K_t = ∅ target contributes 0 to the eligible statistic
   138	     and is dropped from that replicate's usable statistic (matching the
   139	     estimators). Both variants reported. Interval: target-cluster
   140	     bootstrap 95%.
   141	  P5 FPR_Gaussian acceptance: {D2 arm A nulls, rule 1, exact one-sided CP
   142	     upper at observed x <= 0.5%} — the sole confirmatory decision.
   143	No claim direction reversal, endpoint swap, or denominator swap after the
   144	first campaign L-S run.
   145	
   146	## Units of analysis and intervals
   147	
   148	- D1/D3: the star is the unit. Wilson 95% on unweighted proportions; plain
   149	  Wilson on the negatives class (weights cancel); survey bootstrap for PPV;
   150	  ESS-Wilson only for other descriptive weighted proportions, labeled
   151	  approximate.
   152	- D2: the TESS target (TIC) is the CLUSTER; inference is CONDITIONAL on the
   153	  frozen window assignment (report unique window count and reuse table —
   154	  windows repeat across targets, and a target-only bootstrap does not
   155	  represent the 928-window frame; stated as a limitation).
   156	  Estimator: per-target mean over its replicates within a scenario/stratum;
   157	  aggregate = equal-weight mean over the 103 targets (a scenario mix, NOT
   158	  the 928-window frame). Bootstrap: resample the 103 TICs with replacement
   159	  (B = 2000, frozen seed 20260830), carrying ALL of a resampled target's
   160	  replicates, paired census/L-S outcomes, phases, and scenario results
   161	  jointly; identical resample draws across scenarios (common random
   162	  numbers). Percentile 95% intervals; if a statistic is degenerate
   163	  (all-0/all-1), report the exact one-sided CP bound at the target level
   164	  instead. Pooled exact McNemar is PROHIBITED for D2; use the target-cluster
   165	  paired-difference bootstrap.
   166	- Sensitivity contrasts (D2 ladder, phase draws, amplitude-stationarity,
   167	  dominant-mode dropout — ALL core and binding; the ±30% multiplier is a
   168	  local sensitivity, never presented as an astrophysical uncertainty
   169	  envelope):
   170	  COMMON-SUBSET RULE — every contrast against nominal is computed with
   171	  nominal re-evaluated on the same median-window (K=1) subset and the same
   172	  bootstrap draws. Min-max across the 3x3 grid is a "prespecified
   173	  finite-grid sensitivity range", never a confidence band; endpoint
   174	  scenarios identified. De-dilution and amplitude-stationarity are separate
   175	  axes.
   176	
   177	## Complementarity (census vs L-S)
   178	
   179	Per dataset, on labeled positives with both methods available and usable:
   180	C = census flag; L = rule-1 detection (detection-only, symmetric margins).
   181	Report the full 2x2, both discordant fractions, union completeness, and
   182	incremental yields with intervals (Wilson for D1/D3; cluster bootstrap for
   183	D2). Exact McNemar secondary (D1/D3 only; marginal homogeneity, not
   184	complementarity).
   185	
   186	## Surfaces
   187	
   188	Surfaces exist for D2 and D3 only (D1 has no amplitude axis). Two
   189	endpoints, separate files: (a) rule-1 DETECTION completeness over ALL
   190	labeled positives — stars without a defined amplitude (the 154 unjoined
   191	D3 positives) fall in an explicit `amp_unknown` bin (bin index −1), so
   192	the full 610-star denominator is preserved; (b) frequency recovery over
   193	the scorable subset only. Coordinates per star (frozen): D3 = dominant Mo
   194	mode (period from dominant frequency; historical Kepler-band dominant
   195	amplitude, mmag — explicitly non-contemporaneous, not a ZTF-g threshold);
   196	D2 = largest-amplitude RETAINED injected mode (period; published TESS
   197	amplitude, ppt). Bins half-open [lo, hi); explicit underflow and overflow
   198	bins; no smoothing, no monotonic fitting, no interpolation. Edges frozen:
   199	period {100 s, 200 s, 500 s, 1000 s, 2000 s, 0.05 d, 0.2 d, 1 d, 10 d,
   200	100 d}; amplitude D3 {0.5, 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50} mmag with top bin
   201	[50, inf); D2 {0.5, 2, 5, 10, 30} ppt with top bin [30, inf);
   202	median-exposures-per-night {1, 1.5, 2, 3, 5} with top bin [5, inf).
   203	Cells below 5 stars: counts only. Amplitude axes are invariant across
   204	scenarios (never the ladder-scaled injected amplitude).
   205	
   206	## Eligibility and attrition
   207	
   208	Both denominators always reported (see detection completeness). Attrition
   209	table (roster -> fetched -> crossmatched -> QC-passed -> both-passes) by
   210	class, amplitude stratum (including `amp_unknown`), Mo-join status,
   211	magnitude, dominant period, Teff (declared the color surrogate — Murphy
   212	carries no color column and Teff is its physical equivalent), and crowding
   213	(cone object count, nearest-separation). The negative-sample balance
   214	diagnostic (sampled vs full-frame quantiles of gmag/Teff/RA/Dec) is part
   215	of the roster report (`roster_report.json`) and is a required output. D3 near-saturation strata: g <= 14.0 flagged,
   216	g > 14.0 safe (boundary in the flagged stratum). Unavailable passes never
   217	silently dropped; missing light curves enter eligible-roster estimands as
   218	non-detections.
   219	
   220	## Guards
   221	
   222	- Assert no campaign census ratio equals 2.5 exactly.
   223	- Assert every scored JSON has complete == true, both passes present.
   224	- D2 truth ONLY from injected_modes.csv; assert every scored D2 shard id
   225	  appears there (or is a null/control).
   226	- Manifest: SHA-256 of every input file, env versions, frozen + campaign
   227	  file SHAs, replay attestation reference, spec file SHA-256.
   228	- D2 contract (Amendment 2): shard_manifest.csv has the fixed typed schema
   229	  d2_truth_model.MANIFEST_COLUMNS with every field populated for every arm
   230	  (no NaN in int/bool columns; empty strings for absent ids); scenario
   231	  identity is the manifest `scenario` code AND every grouping key (arm,
   232	  ratio_g, ratio_rg, phase_draw, amp_scale, dominant_dropped, cadence_code
   233	  — Amendment 3) — the
   234	  dominant-mode-dropout variant is its own scenario and never enters the
   235	  nominal P4 estimator; the P4 eligible denominator is the scenario's
   236	  `n_strata_scheduled` (3 nominal; 1 for single-window sensitivities), and
   237	  the nominal arm-B scenario must hold exactly one replicate per
   238	  (scheduled target, K ∈ {0,1,2}); truth_d2 refuses an unpublished
   239	  (IN_PROGRESS) or undescribed (no generation_manifest.json) generation,
   240	  requires index == manifest == disk id sets, per-shard SHA identity with
   241	  the generation record, A/B ↔ injected_modes bijection with n_modes
   242	  counts, exact null serials 0..999 (production), and a non-production
   243	  generation only under a pilot run manifest; every scored result needs a
   244	  provenance sidecar whose source_id, result SHA, shard SHA, attestation
   245	  SHA and generation id match, else metrics stop; inputs_sha256 carries
   246	  the full chain (truth tables, index, generation manifest, per-shard
   247	  SHAs, generation inputs, run manifest, completion table).
   248	- Pilot rule: run manifests with `pilot: true` (any --limit/--stars-file
   249	  run) yield `confirmatory: false` on every P4/P5 row and
   250	  `confirmatory_allowed: false` in the metrics manifest.
   251	
   252	## Outputs
   253	
   254	`generalization/results/<date>_<dataset>/metrics/`: per_star.csv,
   255	completeness_by_class_pass_rule.csv, contingency_complementarity.json,
   256	trigger_rates.csv, ppv.csv (D3), fp_frequency_distribution.csv,
   257	chance_match.json, surfaces/*.csv, sensitivity.csv, attrition.csv,
   258	d2_cluster_completeness.csv + d2_scenario_contrasts.csv (D2: P4 table and
   259	the paired common-draw scenario-vs-nominal-K=1 contrasts), manifest.json,
   260	inputs_sha256.json.
   261	Figures via plot_generalization.py from these CSVs only.
     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Synthesize D2 exposure shards: DAV truth signals in real ZTF windows.
     3	
     4	Template pool: ALL 928 stars of the published 2026-08-01 catalog — NOT the
     5	510 not-detected subset (G1 referee finding 1: conditioning templates on the
     6	pipeline's own non-detection is a circularity path). Native variability is
     7	handled by frequency-matched scoring plus paired controls. Every shard
     8	preserves the template's real epochs (bjd_tdb), real cadence structure and
     9	real magerr; arms differ in what carries the noise:
    10	
    11	  arm B (92…)  signal added to the REAL ZTF magnitudes — the headline arm
    12	               ("TESS-truth signals injected into real ZTF photometry").
    13	  ctrl (95…)   paired uninjected copy of every unique arm-B template window —
    14	               identifies windows that trigger natively (real variables in
    15	               the pool), so injected-recovery is scored against its own
    16	               window's baseline behavior.
    17	  arm A (93…)  signal added to a synthetic Gaussian floor (median mag +
    18	               N(0, magerr_i)) — diagnostic; separates window effects from
    19	               real-noise effects.
    20	  nulls (94…)  arm-A construction with amplitude_scale = 0 — 1,000 shards
    21	               cycling the 928 windows with distinct noise seeds (windows
    22	               repeat, noise does not). This measures the GAUSSIAN-NULL
    23	               false-alarm rate, not a real-sky FPR (G1 stats finding 11).
    24	
    25	Templates are the ATTESTED per-star exposure shards the frozen pipeline
    26	consumed (`--exposure-stars`), not a re-derivation: every non-modified column
    27	is copied as its ORIGINAL TEXT TOKEN, the model is evaluated on the epochs as
    28	the frozen loader parses them, and each written shard is re-loaded through the
    29	frozen loader and checked bitwise (epochs) before it counts (G3 methods
    30	finding 7 — a 17-significant-digit BJD can re-parse one ulp off on the
    31	production machine, so tokens, not floats, are what is preserved).
    32	
    33	Template matching per target: |median zg mag − target G| <= 0.25 (widened to
    34	0.5, then nearest-9, when the pool is thin — flagged in the manifest);
    35	K=3 at the 10/50/90th percentiles of median-exposures-per-night, because 75%
    36	of zg nights are single-exposure and per-night median subtraction is the
    37	pre-registered dominant penalty (plan risk 3). Ties: stable sort on
    38	(|Δmag|, source_id), then (exp_per_night, source_id) — a total order.
    39	
    40	Run matrix (plan): nominal (1.7, 0.80) on K=3 for arms A+B; every other
    41	scenario on the median template (K=1) only; 1,000 nulls; one control per
    42	unique arm-B window. Targets with ZERO retained modes at nominal cannot be
    43	positives and are excluded from the matrix (recorded in
    44	excluded_targets.csv); dropout is scheduled only for targets with >= 2
    45	retained modes.
    46	
    47	Scenario identity is an explicit immutable code (d2_truth_model.scenario_code)
    48	carried on every manifest row; the manifest schema is fixed
    49	(d2_truth_model.MANIFEST_COLUMNS) and every row of every arm is fully typed.
    50	
    51	Generation discipline (G3 methods finding 3): shards are built into a staging
    52	directory carrying an IN_PROGRESS sentinel, validated (index == manifest ==
    53	disk, bijections, SHAs), described by generation_manifest.json (a generation
    54	id derived from every input SHA + code SHAs + arguments), and only then
    55	published atomically by renaming the staging directory into place. There is
    56	no resume: a generation is all-or-nothing.
    57	
    58	Truth preservation (G2 methods finding 4): every shard's actually-injected
    59	modes (post sinc rejection, with signed factors and phases) go to
    60	injected_modes.csv and the rejected ones to rejected_modes.csv; the metrics
    61	scorer consumes injected_modes.csv, never the original mode table.
    62	
    63	A stratified pilot_shard_index.txt (~150 shards spanning every arm and
    64	scenario, window strata and target amplitudes) is always emitted for the
    65	timing pilot (run it with --stars-file); pilot outputs are never
    66	confirmatory (G3 methods finding 8).
    67	"""
    68	
    69	from __future__ import annotations
    70	
