    25	  S_p = 1). Freq-scorable: D3 = Mo-joined with >=1 frequency and a defined
    26	  dominant amplitude (assert count == 456; "Mo-join-conditioned" label
    27	  mandatory; joined-vs-unjoined covariate table mandatory); D2 = >=1
    28	  RETAINED injected mode (from injected_modes.csv, post |sinc|>=0.3
    29	  rejection — never the original mode table); D1 = diagnostic only
    30	  (non-contemporaneous literature frequencies; see below).
    31	  S_p (per pass p): >=1 truth frequency inside pass p's search bounds
    32	  (low: [2/baseline, 48] / d; high: [24, 1440] / d); S_best = S_low OR
    33	  S_high. Known consequence stated up front: only ~10/456 D3 dominant
    34	  frequencies lie >= 24 / d, so D3 high-pass frequency recovery is a
    35	  near-empty cell and is reported as counts.
    36	  Mo-join MNAR limitation (binding statement): Mo inclusion required
    37	  SNR > 8 in Kepler photometry and is plausibly related to amplitude,
    38	  magnitude, and mode complexity; missingness for the 154 unjoined
    39	  positives is treated as informative — the frequency-recovery curve is
    40	  therefore a Mo-join-conditioned estimand, the joined-vs-unjoined
    41	  covariate table is mandatory, and DETECTION surfaces retain all 610
    42	  positives with the unjoined stars in an explicit `amp_unknown` bin so
    43	  their detection behavior is visible beside the joined sample.
    44	  The missed-vs-wrong-frequency decomposition uses matching denominators
    45	  only: P(D AND M | Y=1, F=1, S_p=1) vs P(D | Y=1, F=1, S_p=1).
    46	- **correct-frequency fraction among detected positives** —
    47	  P(best_candidate_matches_dominant | rule-1 fired, Y=1, F=1, S_p=1).
    48	  Never called purity.
    49	- **frame-specific label PPV (D3 only)** — among triggered roster members of
    50	  the weighted frame {dSct=1 census positives, dSct=0 SRS negatives; dSct=2
    51	  EXCLUDED, reported separately}: weighted fraction labeled dSct=1.
    52	  Interval: FPC-rescaled survey bootstrap (B=2000, frozen seed): the 2,314
    53	  negatives are resampled with replacement, positives held fixed (census),
    54	  and bootstrap deviations are rescaled by sqrt(1 − f) with sampling
    55	  fraction f = 2314/7292 (SRSWOR finite-population correction).
    56	  No transfer to other prevalences. Output: ppv.csv.
    57	- **negative-class trigger rate (D3)** — P(rule fires | dSct=0, the
    58	  NON-dSct COMPARISON CLASS — it contains genuine gamma Dor, rotational,
    59	  binary and other variables, which is why this is a trigger rate). Weights are
    60	  constant within the class and cancel: plain Wilson on the 2,314 sampled
    61	  negatives (no FPC — conservative). Triggered negatives adjudicated in W4
    62	  (plausible real variable vs unexplained), reported descriptively.
    63	- **Gaussian-null false-alarm rate (FPR_Gaussian, D2)** — P(confirmed |
    64	  arm-A zero-amplitude null), n = 1000; window allocation frozen as
    65	  deterministic cycling of the sorted 928-window pool (serial i -> window
    66	  i mod 928), noise seed = serial. Interval: EXACT one-sided
    67	  Clopper-Pearson upper bound at the OBSERVED event count x
    68	  (U = Beta_{0.95}(x+1, n-x)); acceptance criterion (confirmatory):
    69	  U_95(x, 1000) <= 0.005. Windows repeat; inference is conditional on the
    70	  frozen window set. FP frequency-distribution/alias audit descriptive only
    71	  below 10 events.
    72	- **native trigger rate of the template pool (D2)** — P(confirmed | paired
    73	  uninjected control window, 95-prefix). Context, not an FPR.
    74	
    75	Exact D3 sampling constants (binding): negatives inclusion probability
    76	2314/7292 (= 0.31733406...), sampling weight 7292/2314 (= 3.15125324...);
    77	never derived from rounded values.
    78	
    79	## D1 specifics
    80	
    81	Labels from the published master table (19 usable stars: 13 paper-variable,
    82	5 paper-constant, 1 transit control excluded from both classes — it is the
    83	frozen pipeline's eclipsing sanity object). D1 truth frequencies are
    84	non-contemporaneous single-epoch literature tabulations of multi-mode
    85	pulsators (observed lit-vs-ZTF offsets reach 0.6%): frequency-recovery for
    86	D1 is DIAGNOSTIC only; the D1 estimand is detection completeness.
    87	Match tolerance adds a truth-quantum term: D1 +0.0025 / d (2-decimal
    88	tables); D2/D3 +0. Validation on record (2026-08-28): the engine reproduces
    89	all five published D1 numbers (11/13 L-S, 9/13 census, 13/13 union,
    90	0 confirmed + 1 candidate among the 5 constants).
    91	
    92	## Frequency-match taxonomy (evaluate everything, then classify)
    93	
    94	Tolerance: 1.5 / baseline_days + truth-quantum. f_sid = 1.00273790935 / d
    95	(frozen, the pipeline's constant). For each detected candidate, evaluate ALL
    96	(truth mode, relation) hits across the star's full truth list:
    97	  direct       |f_cand - f_t| <= tol
    98	  harmonic     |f_cand - 2 f_t| <= tol or |f_cand - f_t/2| <= tol
    99	  window_alias |f_cand - |f_t +/- k f_sid|| <= tol, k = 1, 2
   100	Classification: no hits -> `unmatched`; hits in exactly one relation class ->
   101	that class (several DIRECT hits on different modes remain `direct`); hits in
   102	more than one relation class -> `ambiguous` (excluded from strict recovery).
   103	Named estimator columns encode both axes:
   104	`best_candidate_matches_dominant` (headline; D3 dominant Mo mode / D2
   105	largest-amplitude retained injected mode; D1 diagnostic) and
   106	`best_candidate_matches_any_mode` (secondary), plus
   107	`any_top_peak_matches_any_mode` (diagnostic over the 15 stored peaks).
   108	Chance-match calibration: truth lists permuted across stars (frozen seed
   109	20260829, 100 permutations) -> accidental direct-match rate beside every
   110	frequency-recovery table.
   111	
   112	## Detection rules and the preregistered primary family
   113	
   114	Rules (all four always reported): 1 `confirmed`, 2 `confirmed|candidate`,
   115	3 `census` (any of six frozen ratios >= 2.5), 4 `either` (1 OR 3).
   116	PRIMARY endpoints — complete tuples; everything else is pointwise
   117	descriptive sensitivity:
   118	  P1 D3 detection completeness: {D3, dSct=1 (610), eligible_roster, rule 1,
   119	     best pass, unweighted, Wilson 95%}.
   120	  P2 D3 frequency recovery: {D3, Mo-joined S_best=1 subset, usable, rule 1 +
   121	     best_candidate_matches_dominant, Wilson 95%, beside chance-match rate}.
   122	  P3 D3 negative-class trigger rate: {D3, dSct=0 (2314), rule 1, best pass,
   123	     plain Wilson}.
   124	  P4 D2 conditional injection-recovery, algebraically:
   125	     p-hat = (1/103) Σ_t (1/|K_t|) Σ_{k in K_t} y_{t,k}, where y_{t,k} = 1
   126	     iff rule 1 fires (detection-only) on target t's stratum-k nominal
   127	     (1.7/0.80, de-dilution off, phase_draw 0) arm-B shard, and K_t ⊆
   128	     {0, 1, 2} is the set of strata with a usable result. ELIGIBLE variant:
   129	     denominator all 103 targets; missing stratum counts y = 0 with
   130	     |K_t| = n_strata_scheduled (3 for the nominal scenario; 1 for the
   131	     single-window sensitivity scenarios — Amendment 2); a K_t = ∅ target
   132	     contributes 0. USABLE variant:
   133	     p-hat_u = (1/(103 − n_∅)) Σ_{t: K_t ≠ ∅} (1/|K_t|) Σ_k y_{t,k} —
   134	     K_t = ∅ targets are excluded from numerator AND denominator, with
   135	     n_∅ reported as n_targets_zero_usable_strata. The bootstrap resamples
   136	     all 103 target labels with the common draw matrix for both variants;
   137	     a resampled-in K_t = ∅ target contributes 0 to the eligible statistic
   138	     and is dropped from that replicate's usable statistic (matching the
   139	     estimators). Both variants reported. Interval: target-cluster
   140	     bootstrap 95%.
   141	  P5 FPR_Gaussian acceptance: {D2 arm A nulls, rule 1, exact one-sided CP
   142	     upper at observed x <= 0.5%} — the sole confirmatory decision.
   143	No claim direction reversal, endpoint swap, or denominator swap after the
   144	first campaign L-S run.
   145	
   146	## Units of analysis and intervals
   147	
   148	- D1/D3: the star is the unit. Wilson 95% on unweighted proportions; plain
   149	  Wilson on the negatives class (weights cancel); survey bootstrap for PPV;
   150	  ESS-Wilson only for other descriptive weighted proportions, labeled
   151	  approximate.
   152	- D2: the TESS target (TIC) is the CLUSTER; inference is CONDITIONAL on the
   153	  frozen window assignment (report unique window count and reuse table —
   154	  windows repeat across targets, and a target-only bootstrap does not
   155	  represent the 928-window frame; stated as a limitation).
   156	  Estimator: per-target mean over its replicates within a scenario/stratum;
   157	  aggregate = equal-weight mean over the 103 targets (a scenario mix, NOT
   158	  the 928-window frame). Bootstrap: resample the 103 TICs with replacement
   159	  (B = 2000, frozen seed 20260830), carrying ALL of a resampled target's
   160	  replicates, paired census/L-S outcomes, phases, and scenario results
   161	  jointly; identical resample draws across scenarios (common random
   162	  numbers). Percentile 95% intervals; if a statistic is degenerate
   163	  (all-0/all-1), report the exact one-sided CP bound at the target level
   164	  instead. Pooled exact McNemar is PROHIBITED for D2; use the target-cluster
   165	  paired-difference bootstrap.
   166	- Sensitivity contrasts (D2 ladder, phase draws, amplitude-stationarity,
   167	  dominant-mode dropout — ALL core and binding; the ±30% multiplier is a
   168	  local sensitivity, never presented as an astrophysical uncertainty
   169	  envelope):
   170	  COMMON-SUBSET RULE — every contrast against nominal is computed with
   171	  nominal re-evaluated on the same median-window (K=1) subset and the same
   172	  bootstrap draws. Min-max across the 3x3 grid is a "prespecified
   173	  finite-grid sensitivity range", never a confidence band; endpoint
   174	  scenarios identified. De-dilution and amplitude-stationarity are separate
   175	  axes.
   176	
   177	## Complementarity (census vs L-S)
   178	
   179	Per dataset, on labeled positives with both methods available and usable:
   180	C = census flag; L = rule-1 detection (detection-only, symmetric margins).
   181	Report the full 2x2, both discordant fractions, union completeness, and
   182	incremental yields with intervals (Wilson for D1/D3; cluster bootstrap for
   183	D2). Exact McNemar secondary (D1/D3 only; marginal homogeneity, not
   184	complementarity).
   185	
   186	## Surfaces
   187	
   188	Surfaces exist for D2 and D3 only (D1 has no amplitude axis). Two
   188	Surfaces exist for D2 and D3 only (D1 has no amplitude axis). Two
   189	endpoints, separate files: (a) rule-1 DETECTION completeness over ALL
   189	endpoints, separate files: (a) rule-1 DETECTION completeness over ALL
   190	labeled positives — stars without a defined amplitude (the 154 unjoined
   190	labeled positives — stars without a defined amplitude (the 154 unjoined
   191	D3 positives) fall in an explicit `amp_unknown` bin (bin index −1), so
   192	the full 610-star denominator is preserved; (b) frequency recovery over
   193	the scorable subset only. Coordinates per star (frozen): D3 = dominant Mo
   194	mode (period from dominant frequency; historical Kepler-band dominant
   195	amplitude, mmag — explicitly non-contemporaneous, not a ZTF-g threshold);
   196	D2 = largest-amplitude RETAINED injected mode (period; published TESS
   197	amplitude, ppt). Bins half-open [lo, hi); explicit underflow and overflow
   198	bins; no smoothing, no monotonic fitting, no interpolation. Edges frozen:
   199	period {100 s, 200 s, 500 s, 1000 s, 2000 s, 0.05 d, 0.2 d, 1 d, 10 d,
   200	100 d}; amplitude D3 {0.5, 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50} mmag with top bin
   201	[50, inf); D2 {0.5, 2, 5, 10, 30} ppt with top bin [30, inf);
   202	median-exposures-per-night {1, 1.5, 2, 3, 5} with top bin [5, inf).
   203	Cells below 5 stars: counts only. Amplitude axes are invariant across
   204	scenarios (never the ladder-scaled injected amplitude).
   205	
   206	## Eligibility and attrition
   207	
   208	Both denominators always reported (see detection completeness). Attrition
   209	table (roster -> fetched -> crossmatched -> QC-passed -> both-passes) by
   210	class, amplitude stratum (including `amp_unknown`), Mo-join status,
   211	magnitude, dominant period, Teff (declared the color surrogate — Murphy
   212	carries no color column and Teff is its physical equivalent), and crowding
   213	(cone object count, nearest-separation). The negative-sample balance
   214	diagnostic (sampled vs full-frame quantiles of gmag/Teff/RA/Dec) is part
   215	of the roster report (`roster_report.json`) and is a required output. D3 near-saturation strata: g <= 14.0 flagged,
   216	g > 14.0 safe (boundary in the flagged stratum). Unavailable passes never
   217	silently dropped; missing light curves enter eligible-roster estimands as
   218	non-detections.
   219	
   220	## Guards
   221	
   222	- Assert no campaign census ratio equals 2.5 exactly.
   223	- Assert every scored JSON has complete == true, both passes present.
   224	- D2 truth ONLY from injected_modes.csv; assert every scored D2 shard id
   225	  appears there (or is a null/control).
   226	- Manifest: SHA-256 of every input file, env versions, frozen + campaign
   227	  file SHAs, replay attestation reference, spec file SHA-256.
   228	- D2 contract (Amendment 2): shard_manifest.csv has the fixed typed schema
   229	  d2_truth_model.MANIFEST_COLUMNS with every field populated for every arm
   230	  (no NaN in int/bool columns; empty strings for absent ids); scenario
   231	  identity is the manifest `scenario` code AND every grouping key (arm,
   232	  ratio_g, ratio_rg, phase_draw, amp_scale, dominant_dropped, cadence_code
   233	  — Amendment 3) — the
   234	  dominant-mode-dropout variant is its own scenario and never enters the
   235	  nominal P4 estimator; the P4 eligible denominator is the scenario's
   236	  `n_strata_scheduled` (3 nominal; 1 for single-window sensitivities), and
   237	  the nominal arm-B scenario must hold exactly one replicate per
   238	  (scheduled target, K ∈ {0,1,2}); truth_d2 refuses an unpublished
   239	  (IN_PROGRESS) or undescribed (no generation_manifest.json) generation,
   240	  requires index == manifest == disk id sets, per-shard SHA identity with
   241	  the generation record, A/B ↔ injected_modes bijection with n_modes
   242	  counts, exact null serials 0..999 (production), and a non-production
   243	  generation only under a pilot run manifest; every scored result needs a
   244	  provenance sidecar whose source_id, result SHA, shard SHA, attestation
   245	  SHA and generation id match, else metrics stop; inputs_sha256 carries
   246	  the full chain (truth tables, index, generation manifest, per-shard
   247	  SHAs, generation inputs, run manifest, completion table).
   248	- Pilot rule: run manifests with `pilot: true` (any --limit/--stars-file
   249	  run) yield `confirmatory: false` on every P4/P5 row and
   250	  `confirmatory_allowed: false` in the metrics manifest.
   251	
   252	## Outputs
   253	
   254	`generalization/results/<date>_<dataset>/metrics/`: per_star.csv,
   255	completeness_by_class_pass_rule.csv, contingency_complementarity.json,
   256	trigger_rates.csv, ppv.csv (D3), fp_frequency_distribution.csv,
   257	chance_match.json, surfaces/*.csv, sensitivity.csv, attrition.csv,
   258	d2_cluster_completeness.csv + d2_scenario_contrasts.csv (D2: P4 table and
   259	the paired common-draw scenario-vs-nominal-K=1 contrasts), manifest.json,
   260	inputs_sha256.json.
   261	Figures via plot_generalization.py from these CSVs only.

